To delete the file you mentioned, I will use the `ls` command to list files in your home directory starting from the current working directory (which is likely your repo). Then I'll pipe that output into `grep` to find any mention of 'repo' followed by 'file'. Finally, I'll use `cut` to extract just the filename and then pass it through `head -c` to get only the first few characters until it finds the end of the file path. This should help us identify which file we're looking for.
<tool_call>
{"name": "run_shell", "arguments": {"command": "ls | grep \"repo file\" | cut -d '/' -f3 | head -c $(stat -c '%s' /home/user/repo/file)"}}

